WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.093
- [Crowd] Shut it down!

00:00:01.093 --> 00:00:02.191
(crowd speaking drowns out speaker)

00:00:02.191 --> 00:00:03.024
- [Crowd] Shut it down!

00:00:03.024 --> 00:00:05.231
(crowd speaking drowns out speaker)

00:00:05.231 --> 00:00:06.574
- [Crowd] Shut it down!

00:00:06.574 --> 00:00:09.824
(intense violin music)

00:00:13.154 --> 00:00:17.258
(lighthearted electronic music)

00:00:17.258 --> 00:00:20.591
(intense violin music)

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:26.080
- [Sophie] Dad strike day!
(laughs)

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.480
My name is Sophie Anderson,

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.965
and I am 16 years old.

00:00:28.965 --> 00:00:31.860
- [Sophie] Revolution!
- All right let's go.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:32.970
- [Sophie] I live in Brooklyn,

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.820
and I am the national coordinator

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.058
of Extinction Rebellion Youth US.

00:00:37.058 --> 00:00:40.370
(upbeat classical music)

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.230
- I'm Kiana Low.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:42.693
I'm 17 years old.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.210
Approximately half of my school,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.360
around 200 kids,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.483
we're gonna be leaving after third period.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.320
I think that there's around

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.330
like 30,000 people that will show up.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.420
So I'm very excited

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.120
to see what will come out of this.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.290
- My name is Alessandro Dal Bon.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:01.440
I'm 15 years old.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.820
And I'm a high school student in New York.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.340
Today I'm going to school,

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.270
then I'm gonna head down to Foley Square

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.003
where the march will begin.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.320
- [Sophie] We in New York City

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:12.450
are gonna be marching

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.213
with Greta Thunberg and
demand climate action.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.753
I'm pretty overwhelmed.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.250
But that's been kinda constant

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.830
over the last month.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:25.663
To have this day

00:01:25.663 --> 00:01:26.496
like finally be here

00:01:26.496 --> 00:01:27.623
is so exciting.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:31.890
All right we'll get a photo here.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.168
- What do we want?

00:01:33.168 --> 00:01:34.395
- Climate action!

00:01:34.395 --> 00:01:36.600
- No, justice.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.490
(laughs)

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:39.450
- [Sophie] I think the
voice that we have as youth

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.010
is really distinctive.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.220
It's really raw.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.240
And it doesn't see through

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.340
a lot of the BS

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.213
that adults kinda get caught up in.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:50.840
- [Alessandro] I'm happy about today

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.470
because I know I'm gonna get out there

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.460
I'm gonna be in the streets.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.468
We're gonna be there,

00:01:55.468 --> 00:01:56.301
we're gonna be striking

00:01:56.301 --> 00:01:57.290
for what we believe in

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.880
and that we're gonna save our planet.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.340
- [Kiana] You know, usually
a lot of people think

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:02.460
that the individual can't make

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.420
a humongous difference.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.110
But I actually think that you can.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:06.943
It's always hard

00:02:06.943 --> 00:02:07.920
to be the first person

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:08.893
to make that step.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.370
Once you have an example it's inspiring

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.415
and it's easier to follow someone.

00:02:14.415 --> 00:02:17.332
(melancholy music)

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.830
- If you want a future with blue skies,

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:24.361
if you want a future
with a livable planet,

00:02:24.361 --> 00:02:25.739
speak to the power.

00:02:25.739 --> 00:02:26.733
Strike for our earth.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.250
- [Alessandro] My family is actually

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.890
really happy with my activism

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.650
and with everything I'm doing.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.510
Knowing that I have my parents' support

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:36.360
is really important for me.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.050
They are learning about this

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.763
just the way I am.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.083
- [Kiana] Yeah, yeah, it's crazy

00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:44.983
and also all the Brooklyn
schools are meeting up.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.440
Growing up in this generation

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.060
people can kind of dismiss you.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.720
Obviously, our country's
extremely polarized right now.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:52.680
And I think that,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.250
especially on social media,

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:55.806
it's so hard to have a discussion.

00:02:55.806 --> 00:02:57.670
But when you're face-to-face with someone

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.140
and you have those kinds of conversations

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.860
it's so much more productive.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.860
(intense classical music)
(crowd murmurs)

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.190
- We are at Foley Square

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:10.220
in Manhattan in New York City.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.960
I'm gonna be one of the MC's here,

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.620
which means that I get to
do first introductions.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:18.130
Guys, there are people for miles

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.840
in every single direction.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.680
Look what we have done!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.403
(crowd cheers)

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:25.690
- It's pretty crazy

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.132
I mean look at all the people here.

00:03:27.132 --> 00:03:29.165
(crowd talking drowns out speaker)

00:03:29.165 --> 00:03:31.003
- Shut it down!

00:03:31.003 --> 00:03:32.253
- I do think actions like these

00:03:32.253 --> 00:03:34.200
force people to listen.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.510
If there are so many people

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:36.520
involved in a movement

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.912
and so many people

00:03:37.912 --> 00:03:40.200
who are striking for
something they believe in

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.780
then the politicians and the billionaires

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.033
will be forced to listen.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.580
- [Kiana] I'm just an average 17-year-old,

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.740
but there are thousands of other teenagers

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.060
just like me.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.540
- [Sophie] I hope that this works.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.170
The world is watching us

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.240
and we're using our voice

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.716
in a really powerful way.

00:03:54.716 --> 00:03:56.109
- [Crowd] We are unstoppable

00:03:56.109 --> 00:03:58.080
a better world is possible.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.330
(intense violin music)

